Hi, when I read the source code, I happened to notice this
https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/ff2a7929235257642d8f63edb1c580347307f3ee/transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/nio/NioEventLoop.java#L669-L674
The `eventLoop == null` is unnecessary. Although the c2 compiler optimizes it, c1 doesn’t seem to optimize it. Though it’s a small problem，it doesn’t look elegant enough.

equivalent
```java
if (eventLoop == this) {
    unsafe.close(unsafe.voidPromise());
}
return;
```
